# Context as Code (Velura)

Do not invent a second process. Do not create `docs/KAN-n.md` or a parallel context repo.

When starting a task:

1. Run `git log --oneline --show-notes --grep=KAN-n` (or `git log origin/develop..HEAD`).
2. Read `git show --stat <sha>` for the files you will touch.
3. Read **interfaces / JSDoc** in those files — that is the business contract.
4. Open the GitLab MR for that KAN key if the "why" is not in the commit body or git notes.

`AGENTS.md` is the map. Lasting one-line rules: `docs/adr/README.md`. Version history is git + MR, not a new markdown file.

After finishing work: JSDoc on public symbols, commit `KAN-n why`, MR template `## Why`, optional `sh deploy/scripts/git-notes.sh add`.
